src/KOKKOS/atom_vec_ellipsoid_kokkos.cpp:215-218 (AtomVecEllipsoidKokkos_PackCommBonus ctor) and 276-279 (UnpackCommBonus ctor):
    const int size_forward = atomKK->avecKK->size_forward;
    const size_t maxsend = (buf.view<DeviceType>().extent(0)*buf.view<DeviceType>().extent(1))/size_forward;
    const size_t elements = size_forward;
    buffer_view<DeviceType>(_buf,buf,maxsend,elements);
while the offset is computed as (lines 239-240 / 299-300)
    int offset = size_forward - size_forward_bonus;
    if (vel_flag) offset += size_velocity;
and the caller AtomVecKokkos_PackCommVel (src/KOKKOS/atom_vec_kokkos.cpp:824-826) uses
    const size_t elements = atomKK->avecKK->size_forward + atomKK->avecKK->size_velocity;
For ellipsoid size_forward = 3+4 = 7 (src/atom_vec_ellipsoid.cpp:45 size_forward_bonus=4, src/atom_vec.cpp:2483-2491) and size_velocity = 3+3 = 6 (fields_comm_vel={"angmom"}), so with vel_flag=1 the functor indexes _buf(i,9..12) on a view that is only 7 columns wide - i.e. it writes into row i+1, columns 2..5, which pack_comm_vel_kokkos filled with x/v of the next atom.

