`LC_ALL=C grep -n '[^ -~\t]' src/KOKKOS/atom_vec_*_kokkos.{cpp,h}` reports exactly this one line.  .github/copilot-instructions.md: '7-bit US-ASCII everywhere (sources, docs, scripts); Unicode is forbidden (security policy) and fails CI.'

src/KOKKOS/atom_vec_ellipsoid_kokkos.cpp:186-187:
  Sorter.sort(LMPDeviceType(), d_ellipsoid);
  Sorter.sort(LMPDeviceType(), d_bonus);
Sorting d_ellipsoid moves the bonus *indices* along with their atoms, which is already correct; additionally permuting d_bonus by the same atom permutation destroys the ellipsoid[i] -> bonus mapping (bonus is a compacted array of nlocal_bonus <= nlocal entries) and no bonus[k].ilocal is updated afterwards.  `d_bonus` is declared in atom_vec_ellipsoid_kokkos.h:118 but never assigned - grow_bonus() (lines 157-168) only calls memoryKK->grow_kokkos(k_bonus,bonus).  The code is currently unreachable because AtomKokkos::sort (src/KOKKOS/atom_kokkos.cpp:345-353) forces sort_legacy = true for any bonus style.

src/KOKKOS/atom_vec_ellipsoid_kokkos.cpp:469 (_buf(buf)) and 539 (_buf(buf)) take buf.view_host()/view_device() unchanged, so the row stride is whatever extent(1) the DualView happens to have.  AtomVecKokkos_UnpackBorderVel instead re-views it (src/KOKKOS/atom_vec_kokkos.cpp:2045-2047):
    const size_t elements = atomKK->avecKK->size_border + atomKK->avecKK->size_velocity;
    _buf = typename AT::t_double_2d_lr_const_um(buf.data(),maxsend,elements);
and CommKokkos::grow_recv_kokkos (src/KOKKOS/comm_kokkos.cpp:1906-1909) always allocates k_buf_recv with extent(1) = size_border, never size_border+size_velocity, while grow_send_kokkos (1877-1894) does widen k_buf_send under ghost_velocity.  The two therefore disagree for the remote-receive path with ghost velocities.

src/KOKKOS/comm_kokkos.cpp:1110-1115:
  // clear global->local map for owned and ghost atoms
  // b/c atoms migrate to new procs in exchange() and new ghosts are created in borders()
  // map_set() is done at end of borders()
  if (lmp->kokkos->atom_map_legacy)
    if (map_style != Atom::MAP_NONE) atom->map_clear();
The CPU base has no such guard, src/comm_brick.cpp:614: 'if (map_style != Atom::MAP_NONE) atom->map_clear();'.  The device rebuild in src/KOKKOS/atom_map_kokkos.cpp:217-256 clears only the hash:
  auto& d_map_hash = k_map_hash.view_device();
  if (!map_style_array) d_map_hash.clear();
  ... if (map_style_array) d_map_array(tag_i) = i;
so entries of d_map_array whose tag is no longer owned or ghosted on this rank keep the value written at an earlier map_set().  Consumers rely on -1, e.g. src/KOKKOS/neigh_bond_kokkos.cpp:313-317:
  int atom1 = AtomKokkos::map_kokkos<DeviceType>(bond_atom(i,m),map_style,k_map_array,k_map_hash);
  if (atom1 == -1) { nmissing++; ... }

