src/KOKKOS/comm_kokkos.cpp:1895-1899:
  maxsend = static_cast<int> (BUFFACTOR * n);
  int maxsend_border = (maxsend+Comm::BUFEXTRA)/atomKK->avecKK->size_border;
versus src/comm_brick.cpp:1426-1437, which allocates 'maxsend+bufextra' where src/comm.cpp:272 sets 'bufextra = maxexchange + BUFEXTRA'.  CommBrick::exchange() packs one atom (up to maxexchange doubles) past the point where it last checked 'if (nsend > maxsend) grow_send(nsend,1)', so the headroom must be >= maxexchange, not the fixed 1000 of BUFEXTRA (further reduced by the integer division by size_border).

